%% Delivery flow as verified in AWS (2026-11-23): from pull request to a running, verified release.
%% Every arrow into AWS uses short-lived OIDC credentials; every change to AWS has a human approval.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Dev as Developer
  participant GH as GitHub (PR + ruleset)
  participant CI as ci.yml (no AWS access)
  participant IB as image-build.yml
  participant ECR as ECR (immutable)
  actor Owner as Owner (reviewer)
  participant AD as app-deploy.yml
  participant ECS as ECS Fargate + ALB
  participant CW as CloudWatch / SNS

  Dev->>GH: pull request (code + service.yaml)
  GH->>CI: tests, Ruff, Bandit, Terraform tests, TFLint, Checkov, Trivy
  CI-->>GH: ci-ok (required) - insecure change = red, merge blocked
  Dev->>GH: merge to main
  GH->>IB: build, hardened smoke test, Trivy gate, SBOM
  IB->>ECR: push git-<commit> (single manifest), publish sha256 digest
  Dev->>AD: run with image digest
  AD->>Owner: wait for dev-deploy approval
  Owner-->>AD: approve (reject = job never starts, no credentials)
  AD->>ECS: new task-definition revision, only the image changed
  ECS-->>AD: rollout COMPLETED + healthy target (or FAILED -> circuit breaker rollback)
  ECS->>CW: deployment events, JSON logs, alarms -> e-mail
